* >Natural Source Header 000000
* :Mode S
* :CP
* :LineIncrement 5
* <Natural Source Header
* RMSCBS2 - Scan BS2 Queue and Create Source and Orders
*           Since Spool version 3.0 BS2000 allows to define a device
*           APPLICATION. This module is for compatibility to all
*           previous versions of BS2000 spool
*
* Note         since s(211638) 4 NOM devices can be defined to decide
*              which kind of cc type is contained in the spool file.
*              DEVICE (1) -> cc type is taken from the print file's
*                            recform (recform=(v,m), ...)
*              DEVICE (2) -> cc is EBCDIC (space=e)
*              DEVICE (3) -> cc is ASA (space=a)
*              DEVICE (4) -> cc is IBM Machine code (space=i)
*
* Note         since s(9999999) a new ESY feature is used to optimize
*              access to the spool-queue (for Version 9.5 and Version
*              10) and to allow selection for spool queue entries
*              belonging to local destinations or devices (Version 10).
*              This feature is activated by the use of a new field
*              INFO-TYPE in the View SPOOL-QUEUE.
*
*              FIND SPOOL-QUEUE
*                   WITH INFO-TYPE = 'OLD'
*                   AND  type-number = 7
*                   AND  DEVICE      = <device>
*              results in a /STA L,TYPE=7,DEVICE=<device>
*              It seems that a selection for destination isn't
*              working so that we have to select it by prefixing
*              the device with '*'. (Version independent, RSO only)
*
*              FIND SPOOL-QUEUE
*                   WITH INFO-TYPE = 'ORIGIN' /* or 'DEST'
*                   AND  DEVICE      = <device> /* or DESTINATION = ...
*              results in a /SH-JOB-JOB-STA INF=<info-type>, ...
*              (Version 10, local and remote devices/destinations)
*              The use of TYPE-NUMBER is not allowed !!!!!!!!
*
*              It is not allowed to specify more than one device/
*              destination at a time (OR = )
*
* Note         A BS2000 File name consits of a pubset, userid and
*              filename token. (:PPPP:$UUUUUUUU.<filename>).
*              <filename>                  max. 41
*              <UUUUUUUU>                  max. 8
*              <PPPP>                      max. 4
*              :PPPP:$UUUUUUUU.<filename>  max. 54
*
* Maintenance
* uuu yy-mm-dd s(999999)  ...
* mrs 95-09-27 s(999999) clean up (NOM135)
* gw  96-02-12 s(999999) user exits
* mwi 96-06-14 s(999999) nat1305 if record-length > 999
* gw  96-06-15 s(999999) renaming of bs2000 files
* gw  96-06-16 s(999999) allow reprocessing of the same print file
*                        if a source record already exists, we don't
*                        cancel the queue entry, instead we create order
*                        records
* gw  96-11-05 s(256333) trigger processing does not work
* jwo 97-03-10 p(161209) copy   bs2000 files y/n
* mwi 97-03-25 p(263275) let :catid: be a part of the filename
* mrs 97-05-27 p(162737) account information
* jwo 97-06-04 p(162737) missing field CHAR-SET-A moved
* jwo 97-06-04 p(162705) don't process same file twice if RENAME is
*                        activated.
* jwo 97-06-10 p(162903) avoid multiple count orders for same file
* jwo 97-06-10 p(162737) account information read for virt. printer
* jwo 97-11-13 p(167263) add active reports exit
* gw  98-06-22 p(171828) user exit 009 to make count optimization
*                        optional
* jvd 98-09-10 p(164220) NOM141ÖNAT23
* gw  98-11-05 p(164220) OD-PARAMETER redefine
* jvd 99-08-02 p(184925) continue proccessing SPOOL-FILE ever after
*                        in processing FILE-ATTRIBUTES
* sju 00-03-27 p(191368) monitor multitasking
* wcd 00-04-01 CE 7267   re-cat as changes made to EOMRPM-E
* xsiszha 2000-08-15 (CE7461) Extend Report and Bundle Names
* fhi     2000-09-28 QA04     Correct CE7461
* sju     2000-11-30 p(202436) reset idle indicator if work to do
* fhi     2002-06-13 s(225125) Add email notificaton, NOMEX010
* sju     2002-07-05 p(225943) no message if trigger db/file wrong
* fhi     2002-09-25 p(218246) Monitor error recovery
* fhi     2002-11-20 fhi102    NAT0936 occurred because NPR DDMs changed
* sju     2003-06-26 p(230407) Correct setting of retry info in orders
* sju     2004-11-29 nom31     restow for changed NRM-ORDER
* sju 04-12-06 NOM31     Add date and time (tenths of second) to trace
* sju 05-02-18 NOM31     Long records other than JES2
* fhi     2005-06-23 p(266530) Make Monitor NPR Mainframe independent
* fhi     2005-12-05 P272727   Avoid NAT6223 under Unix
* xsetggr 2007-05-02 NOM3201   Support 5 bytes node numbers
* xsetggr 2008-02-14 p(300297) restow due changes in RMSCTR-P
* xsetggr 2008-05-05 p(304350) restow due to changes in RMSPL--L
* fhi     2009-05-19 N3463     Extend metadata for OPO
* fhi     2010-05-12 P325555   Extend trace facility
* xsetggr 2010-05-27 P325643   wrong source rec stored
* fhi     2010-09-03 NOMALL-97 Extend message line
* fhi     2010-10-08 NOMALL-97 Use dynamic memory handling
* fhi     2010-10-12 NOMALL-97 Use trace levels, use XXRLOG, old tags dl
* xsetggr 2010-11-07 NOMALL-877 correct some P325643 changes
* raya    2012-08-20 NOMALL-78  disable long records
* fhi     2012-08-24 NOMALL-1004 Add report formatting
* fhi     2012-10-18 NOMALL-1004 Add report formatting, old tags del.
* raya     2012-11-29 NOMALL-1214 check cat date of nomex*
* xsetggr  2013-01-17 NOMALL-1133 prevent processing double reports when
*                     cancel not yet done for the same device
* fhi      2013-05-06 NOMALL-1004 Issue error if conv source not unique
* raya     2013-05-09 NOMALL-1214 backout check cat date of nomex*
* xsetggr 2013-06-10 NOMALL-1227 process count order,if related source
*                                has sr-number-of-lines = 0
* fhi     2014-03-03 NOMALL-1363 Get cat cate into trace messages
* SU1     2014-11-17 NOMALL-1450 fill fields for Adabas Vista
* SU2     2016-07-21 NOMALL-1860 NOM 3.5: remove OSD from BS2000
* fhi     2016-08-01 NOMALL-1748 Backout Report Formatting
* fhi     2016-12-02 NOMALL-1621 +NOD-* instead of G-MONITOR-NODE       STEM
* fhi     2016-11-15 NOMALL-1961 Use new task IDs
* fhi     2017-01-10 NOMALL-1916 Use node number in report definition
* fhi     2017-01-11 NOMALL-1916 Store codepage in source record
* fhi     2017-01-26 NOMALL-1961 Wake correct monitor task
* fhi     2017-03-31 NOMALL-2009 Improve RDC handling
* fhi     2017-05-02 NOMALL-1917 Use correct conditions for bin fields
* fhi     2017-06-16             Add trace, no tags
* SU3     2018-01-03             NOM 3.5: misc. changes
* fhi     2018-03-13 NOMALL-1918 Correct multinode behavior, no tags
* fhi     2018-03-26 NOMALL-1918 Create load order for remote nodes
* SU4     2018-03-26             avoid NAT3062 on UNIX
* fhi     2018-07-19 NOMALL-2121 Use node number and esyuser
* SU5     2018-08-02 NOMALL-2133 node fallback:use local if none in RP
* fhi     2018-08-06 NOMALL-2135 Use internal node id in orders
* fhi     2018-09-19 NOMALL-2121 Don't throw 7138, instead, do EsyLOGON
* bli     2018-10-10 NOMALL-2061 use codepage function F#GETCP
* fhi     2018-12-14 NOM 3.5     Add CPU measure
* SU6     2019-01-31             avoid 'Defaul' in output
* SU7     2019-03-08 NOMALL-2177 RMSC-C2
* BLI     2020-02-18 NOMALL-2294 Receipt stamp
* SU8     2020-06-22 NOMALL-2349 show full msg
* BLI1    2022-03-09 NOMALL-2533 delete order in case of errors
* BLI2    2022-06-20 NOMALL-2562 Adapt RMRCSTMP job-id
* BLI3    2023-04-14 NOMALL-2616 Warning 7022 when second codepage found
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------
